1. HOLD: Spellcheck — real Hunspell WASM engine. The plugin is wired into the editor
   (createSpellcheckPlugin), but the checker behind it (SimpleSpellChecker,
   packages/app/src/spellcheck/hunspell.ts) is an in-memory word-set placeholder:
   no .dic/.aff loading, and suggest() always returns []. Need to load real
   Hunspell dictionaries per language.
2. HOLD: Language UI (low priority — display-only indicator done; full feature needs design):
   - One-click {lang=} override: right-click context menu, inserts tag at cursor or wraps selection
   - Language tags ({lang=XX}): not yet handled by parser/editor. Need to decide:
     a) AST representation in parser
     b) Editor rendering and preservation of tags
     c) How LanguageContext resolves effective language from tags vs frontmatter
     d) Whether tags apply to inline spans or whole block elements
3. HOLD: Navigator color-coding by tags/location/status — not implemented; only a
   generic accent color exists for hover/selection, not data-driven coloring.
4. HOLD: Watermark for exports — frontmatter watermark: renders on-screen and in
   print/PDF export (workflow-reports.ts), but is not applied in DOCX export
   (docx-exporter.ts). Also no per-export toggle to opt out when the field is
   set — it's implicitly always-on.
6. Extension points: dependency-inject AIProvider, SpeechProvider, and
   SessionContext (OSS spec §11.5). They are type-only in
   packages/editor/src/extensions/types.ts; ai-client.ts and voice-service.ts
   are still imported directly by VoiceToolbar, SettingsDialog, SceneNavigator,
   StatusBar, VoiceConfirmDialog, and OnboardingDialog. Follow the
   StorageAdapter pattern (interface + React context + useXAdapter() hook,
   provider prop on DocumentProvider, concrete default in @sutrata/app).
   SessionContext must actually drive read-only / comment-only modes.
7. Extension points: make PanelRegistry, CommandRegistry, and ExportRegistry
   real. AppShell has a fixed panel set and ExportDialog a fixed format list;
   embedders need to add panels, commands/shortcuts, and export formats
   without forking the editor.
8. Extension points: revise the DecorationProvider and CollabBinding
   signatures before they become stable. DecorationProvider
   (from/to/className per scene) is too thin for comment threads, click
   handlers, and widgets; CollabBinding.bind() gets no editor state or view,
   so nothing can bind to it.
9. @sutrata/extension-testkit (OSS spec §11.1, §11.5): a stub embedder that
   implements every extension point, plus a CI job that builds and tests it
   on every PR. Not present yet.
10. HOLD: @sutrata/cloud-connector (OSS spec §11.1, P2, optional): an open
    StorageAdapter for the documented sync API. Not bundled by default; the
    app must work identically without it.
11. Release process for @sutrata/parser and @sutrata/editor (both published
    to npm; always publish with `pnpm publish` so workspace:* is rewritten).
    Adopt Changesets; the extension API follows semver, with a migration note
    for every breaking change (strict semver from 1.0).
12. HOLD: Stable scene IDs — automatic assignment. {#id} is optional in the
    format, but scene-level diff (§3.5), comments, and any
    production data keyed by scene need every scene to have one. Done: the
    scene navigator marks scenes without an ID (cs-nav-scene-missing-id,
    --cs-ui-warning). On hold: a parser/editor helper (assignSceneIds) that
    assigns IDs as a visible, user-confirmed edit, so every tool uses the same
    ID-generation rule.
13. Revision mode (OSS spec §3.6, P2): not implemented (only locale strings
    exist). Needs a format-spec addition first (attribute or & key scheme for
    revision marks), then revision colors, revision stars on export, page
    locking with A-pages, and OMITTED scenes. Builds on the existing
    "lock scene numbers" action in SceneNavigator.
14. Import (OSS spec §5.5, §5.6, P2): legacy-font → Unicode conversion
    (Krutidev/Shree-Lipi for Hindi, Bamini/TAM/TAB for Tamil, Anu for Telugu
    first; then Nudi/Baraha, ML-TT) and heuristic Word import of arbitrary
    scripts. docx-importer.ts currently handles only Sutrata's own DOCX output.
15. Lossless editor serializer (OSS spec §11.6, P2): prosemirror-to-sutra.ts
    is best-effort. Carry unknown attributes and metadata as node attrs and
    add a property test that parse → PM → serialize → parse yields an equal
    AST over the whole conformance corpus. Required before any real-time
    collaboration (CollabBinding) is used.
